      },
      "derived_from": {
        "@id": "entity:target-pages_originstorypage.peripateticware_doesnt_fully_solve_the_c-v1"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.the_short_answer_is_that_most_of_the_ena-2026-11-25T18:15:25.308276+00:00",
      "@type": "prov:Activity",
      "prov:startTime": "2026-11-25T18:15:25.308276+00:00",
      "actor": {
        "@id": "agent:MICROSOFT-Azure-Cognitive-v3_(unconfigured,_pass-through)_Profile__Technical/Legal_Documentation_|_Temp__0.1"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:target-pages_originstorypage.the_short_answer_is_that_most_of_the_ena-v2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "The short answer is that most of the enabling technology wasn\\'t ready in 2007. GPS in every pocket came first (2010–2015). Then high-quality mobile cameras. Then cloud APIs cheap enough for schools. Then local AI models (Ollama, llama.cpp) that can run on a teacher\\'s home server without a $10,000/month inference bill. The 2007 paper was right about the destination; it couldn\\'t have known how long the road would be.",
      "generated_by": {
        "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.the_short_answer_is_that_most_of_the_ena-2026-11-25T18:15:25.308276+00:00"
      },
      "used_source": {
        "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.the_short_answer_is_that_most_of_the_ena"
      },
      "derived_from": {
        "@id": "entity:target-pages_originstorypage.the_short_answer_is_that_most_of_the_ena-v1"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.the_longer_answer_is_that_educational_te-2026-11-25T18:15:25.308276+00:00",
      "@type": "prov:Activity",
      "prov:startTime": "2026-11-25T18:15:25.308276+00:00",
      "actor": {
        "@id": "agent:MICROSOFT-Azure-Cognitive-v3_(unconfigured,_pass-through)_Profile__Technical/Legal_Documentation_|_Temp__0.1"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:target-pages_originstorypage.the_longer_answer_is_that_educational_te-v3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "The longer answer is that educational technology spent those years solving the wrong problem. EdTech iterated on the classroom — better LMS, better video, better quiz tools. It made the existing model more efficient. Peripateticware doesn\\'t try to make the classroom more efficient. It tries to replace the classroom, at least occasionally, with the world.",
      "generated_by": {
        "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.the_longer_answer_is_that_educational_te-2026-11-25T18:15:25.308276+00:00"
      },
      "used_source": {
        "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.the_longer_answer_is_that_educational_te"
      },
      "derived_from": {
        "@id": "entity:target-pages_originstorypage.the_longer_answer_is_that_educational_te-v2"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.thats_a_harder_sell_schools_are_riskaver-2026-11-25T18:15:25.308276+00:00",
      "@type": "prov:Activity",
      "prov:startTime": "2026-11-25T18:15:25.308276+00:00",
      "actor": {
        "@id": "agent:MICROSOFT-Azure-Cognitive-v3_(unconfigured,_pass-through)_Profile__Technical/Legal_Documentation_|_Temp__0.1"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:target-pages_originstorypage.thats_a_harder_sell_schools_are_riskaver-v2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "That\\'s a harder sell. Schools are risk-averse. Outdoor learning has a liability optic. \"The world is your classroom\" sounds like a marketing line until you\\'ve watched a ten-year-old explain sediment transport to a crow-shaped AI guide while standing in a creek bed, and then read the field journal entry they wrote that afternoon, and understood that they understood.",
      "generated_by": {
        "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.thats_a_harder_sell_schools_are_riskaver-2026-11-25T18:15:25.308276+00:00"
      },
      "used_source": {
        "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.thats_a_harder_sell_schools_are_riskaver"
      },
      "derived_from": {
        "@id": "entity:target-pages_originstorypage.thats_a_harder_sell_schools_are_riskaver-v1"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "activity:translation-team_1_bio-2026-11-25T18:15:25.308276+00:00",
      "@type": "prov:Activity",
      "prov:startTime": "2026-11-25T18:15:25.308276+00:00",
      "actor": {
        "@id": "agent:MICROSOFT-Azure-Cognitive-v3_(unconfigured,_pass-through)_Profile__Technical/Legal_Documentation_|_Temp__0.1"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:target-team_1_bio-v2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "Paul spent a decade as a teacher, four years working for edtechs, and has been experimenting with how to break learning out of books and classrooms for two decades. Peripateticware takes advantage of LLM advancements and leverages mobile technologies to allow students to learn from the world with guidance from their teachers wherever they choose to roam.",
      "generated_by": {
        "@id": "activity:translation-team_1_bio-2026-11-25T18:15:25.308276+00:00"
      },
      "used_source": {
        "@id": "entity:source-team_1_bio"
